faqs:
  - q: When is RPA the wrong answer?
    a: When an API exists. When the upstream system will change in the next quarter. When the process is inconsistent enough that exceptions outnumber the happy path. We will say so.
  - q: How do you decide which processes to automate?
    a: Hours saved, stability of the source system, complexity, and audit exposure. We prefer a small number of high-value bots over many small ones.
  - q: What about AI inside RPA?
    a: Where it adds value. Document understanding, classification, or routing can lift a bot from a rule engine to a real intake layer. Only where the accuracy bar can be met.
  - q: Who runs the bots after you leave?
    a: Your team, or us under managed services. Runbooks and monitoring come with every build.
  - q: Do you rescue existing bot portfolios?
    a: Yes. Audit, rationalize, fix, and often retire a third of what is there. Outcome is usually a healthier smaller portfolio.
